==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmoʊ.ɡəl/|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
The word mogul originally meant [[Mongol]], or person of Mongolian descent. In this context, it refers to the Mughal Empire (mughal being Persian or Arabic for "Mongol") of Indian Subcontinent that existed between 1526 and 1857: the early Mughal emperors claimed a heritage dating back to Mongol ruler Genghis Khan. The modern meaning of the word is supposedly derived from the storied riches of the Mughal emperors, which for example produced the [[w:Taj_Mahal|Taj Mahal]].

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# a [[rich]] or [[powerful]] person; a [[magnate]]

